course: dictionary
lesson: 9140
title: Sneak and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. Sneak is a good example. «Not for playing a demo, his mum said, but for sneaking.» Here sneaking means doing something secretly, something you have been told not to do.
explain: Sneak can mean moving quietly so nobody sees or hears you. «Leah sneaked off to the bouncy castle» means she slipped away without anyone noticing. The words around it tell you it was done quietly and in secret.
explain: Sneak can also be a noun. A sneak is a person who does things secretly or tells tales on others (UK, informal). In «every hunter has its own plan: some chase, some sneak», sneak is a verb: the hunter moves quietly to get close to its food. Swap your meaning into the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Sneak» means to move quietly and secretly so nobody sees or hears you, as in «sneak up on» a friend.
fact: To «sneak» something means to take or do it secretly, as in «sneak a biscuit».
fact: A «sneak» is a person who does things secretly or tells tales on others (UK, informal).
fact: «A sneak peek» is a quick, secret look at something before others see it.
exercise: «Leah sneaked off to the bouncy castle.» What does sneaked off mean here? | Cried because she was sad | *Slipped away quietly, so nobody noticed | Shouted loudly for everyone to join her | Fell asleep on the bouncy castle
exercise: «Not for playing a demo, his mum said, but for sneaking.» What is the sneaking here? | Playing a game with his friends outside | *Doing something he had been told not to do, in secret | Helping his mum cook dinner | Practising a song for the school concert
exercise: Ben says sneak is just a boring word for walk. In «children sneak up behind their friends», what does sneak mean? | Run fast and loudly | Walk very slowly with a limp | Sing a happy song | *Move quietly so nobody sees or hears you
test: «The hunter had to sneak close to its food.» What does sneak mean here? | Set a trap and wait | Eat the food quickly | Chase the food very fast | *Move quietly and secretly to get close
test: Picture the French playground on 1 April. What is the French April fool called? | *Poisson d'avril | Demo | Snuck | Chippy
exam: Which sentence uses sneak as a noun, meaning a person? | I will sneak a look at the answers | *Tom called Sam a sneak for telling tales | Dan likes to sneak up on people | Let's sneak in quietly before the bell
